&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Excerpt from New York Times article, 17 March 2017:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#8230;have reported feeling an urge to read articles published by Elenjepo Publishing upon seeing them, even if they are not something they would normally be interested in. Leading memetics researchers theorize that Elenjepo Publishing is using cognitohazards on their headlines to make consumers feel enticed to read them. Elenjepo Publishing has denied these allegations. The investigation is currently ongoing&amp;#8230;&lt;/p&gt;
