&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Excerpts from&lt;/em&gt; CNN &lt;em&gt;article titled &amp;quot;Verizon stocks continue to drop, outcry towards Tumblr decision reaches federal level&amp;quot;, publication date 7 August 2017:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So far, the month of August has not been kind to Verizon Communications (NYSE:VZ). The company&#039;s decision to suspend two users on its microblogging subsidiary Tumblr last week has been harshly criticized as being transphobic and xenophobic, and the fury doesn&#039;t appear to be slowing down. Tumblr&#039;s user-base, the anomalous social hacktivist group Gamers Against Weed, and now Democratic members of the US Senate and House have all voiced their disapproval&amp;#8230;&lt;/p&gt;
