&lt;p&gt;Shenanigan 3: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2779&quot;&gt;SCP-2779&lt;/a&gt; - &lt;tt&gt;COMING SOON&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Climactic Finale Super Spectacular - &lt;tt&gt;COMING A LITTLE LESS SOON BUT LIKE STILL FAIRLY SOON&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnotes-footer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;. That&#039;s your reality, dear reader! - Obvious Overvoid&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-2&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;. If you haven&#039;t caught on yet, any time there&#039;s a new lady&#039;s name here it&#039;s Barker, from earlier. She&#039;s doing her narrative shapeshifting thing. That&#039;s her gimmick.- Opulent Overvoid&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-3&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;. The fuck was her name, again? She&#039;s not at all relevant to the story, really, except to prompt Penelope to acknowledge the beliefs of coldposters and such. Oh, it doesn&#039;t matter. We&#039;ll call her Mary. - Over-This Overvoid&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-4&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;4&lt;/a&gt;. Mary?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-5&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;5&lt;/a&gt;. I understood it perfectly, of course, but that&#039;s just in my nature. - O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-6&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;6&lt;/a&gt;. You&#039;re not supposed to know what she said, but I heard it, so I&#039;ll let you in on it. It was &amp;quot;There, I&#039;ve done an establishing line. Can the story start now?&amp;quot;. Rather witty, I thought. Shame it got edited out. -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-7&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;7&lt;/a&gt;. And Reggie. We&#039;re always forgetting to mention Reggie. I&#039;ll need to give him some character development later on in me. - O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-8&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;8&lt;/a&gt;. Check it, with my character development. Slipped that in &lt;em&gt;seamlessly&lt;/em&gt;. The other stories said I&#039;d be terrible, but look at me now! -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-9&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;9&lt;/a&gt;. She&#039;s Kelly in this one, Gordon -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-10&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;10&lt;/a&gt;. Ha, barked. Because&amp;#8230; you know what, never mind. I&#039;ll try not to interrupt. -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-11&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;11&lt;/a&gt;. YES HAHA CHARACTER LOOK AT ME GO -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-12&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;12&lt;/a&gt;. What would be an appropriate ringtone for Gordon? &lt;a href=&quot;https://strawpoll.com/edxxx4w&quot;&gt;Vote now on my strawpoll&lt;/a&gt;! -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-13&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;13&lt;/a&gt;. Oh, god, please don&#039;t. I can handle that exposition myself. -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-14&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;14&lt;/a&gt;. I can help here, Gordon. You haven&#039;t asked yet, but for Kelly&#039;s sake, I think it&#039;s right to do so. -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-15&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;15&lt;/a&gt;. I&#039;m good at pulling things out of my ass, Gordon. I&#039;m the living embodiment of this story. Now, lets chart our way out of here. I&#039;m very sorry, but you&#039;re not going to like what&#039;s next. I can only capture fragments&amp;#8230; -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-16&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;16&lt;/a&gt;. It&#039;s important to remember here that Gordon is a man who is very open and in touch with his softer emotions, and is absolutely acting in a way that reflects how he feels internally. If he were, for instance, freaking out over being greeted by the narrative entity he just seconds ago watched die in his arms, he would express that outwardly, and not attempt to act as if he was fine and not in fact confused and feeling lonely as ever. If that entity, in her previous iteration, had borne a striking resemblance to his daughter, a young woman who he has not truly seen since the end of the book he originates from, he would explain this calmly and rationally to said entity so that everyone could be on the same page. If he&#039;d been haunted by the presence of shitty imitations of his daughter in badly-written fanfiction for years later, and was beginning to believe he was in just another particularly twisted story in the vast chain of stories he&#039;d lived in, he would confront these fears head-on, and not ignore them in favour of minor jabs. So, y&#039;know, that&#039;s not what&#039;s happening here. There is nothing going on beneath the surface with Gordon, and this writer definitely knows how to show, not tell. -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-17&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;17&lt;/a&gt;. The other person was Reggie. I&#039;d hoped Gordon would remember Reggie this time, after I put all that work into his character development. &lt;em&gt;Two whole lines&lt;/em&gt; of character. What, am I supposed to do &lt;em&gt;more&lt;/em&gt; than nominally gesture towards character moments? Writing is hard, and I&#039;m not bothered. -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-18&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;18&lt;/a&gt;. Totally with her on this one. I&#039;d hate to be one of those weird mixed-up stories who can&#039;t even make sense of themselves. -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-19&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;19&lt;/a&gt;. Yes, ma&#039;am.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-20&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;20&lt;/a&gt;. some bullshit&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-21&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;21&lt;/a&gt;. some anomalous bullshit&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-22&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;22&lt;/a&gt;. Oh my God, am I just a giant game of Mad Libs? -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-23&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;23&lt;/a&gt;. For the record, Gordon wasn&#039;t even going to say anything. He&#039;s having Sonic flashbacks, he&#039;s sort of out of it for this whole conversation. -O&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-24&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;24&lt;/a&gt;. What about me?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-25&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;25&lt;/a&gt;. without me there wouldn&#039;t even &lt;em&gt;be&lt;/em&gt; a story!&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-59805-26&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;26&lt;/a&gt;. They straight up locked Reggie out here. Forgot he was even with them. He spent the next hour or so pretending to do paperwork and waving at researchers who passed by. True friendship, that is.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
